From 3f019aaec3554ed429630a46e630f969ded5dd62 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Raing5Days <M202574102@hust.edu.cn>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 10:48:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(v1): converge split-batch cudagraph key policy into
 pluggable strategy

Move the DUAL_INPLACE offset / descriptor-aware key construction and
lazy-capture dispatch policy out of the CudagraphDispatcher control flow
into a pluggable CudagraphKeyStrategy component.

Core keeps only the stable seam:
- replay entry point (dispatch signature + BatchDescriptor as versioned
  key metadata, hash/eq lookup unchanged),
- fail-closed eager fallback (no registered key -> CUDAGraphMode.NONE,
  extended metadata preserved on the no-graph descriptor),
- Platform.get_cudagraph_key_strategy() hook (default None).

The transitional InplaceSplitKeyStrategy default replicates the previous
inline behavior exactly; platforms (e.g. vllm-ascend) can take over the
policy by implementing the platform hook, after which the default can be
removed from core. dispatch()'s extended keyword parameters are kept for
out-of-tree caller compatibility (keyword calls + getattr reads).
